    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever wondered how many "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "calories",
            "zh": "卡路里"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are in your lunch? A new app called Cal AI can help. All you have to do is take a photo of your food, and the app will tell you its calorie count. It can also show you the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "nutrients",
            "ref": "v-nutrient"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in your dish, such as "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "protein",
            "ref": "v-protein"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", fat, and sugar."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Cal AI was created by Zach Yadegari, an 18-year-old student. In 2023, Zach tried another calorie-counting app, MyFitnessPal, to track his meals. But typing in everything he ate took too much time. “It was very boring and hard to use,” Zach said. After just three days, he "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "quit",
            "zh": "放弃"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Zach wanted something faster and smarter. So, he teamed up with his high school friends to develop a better app. Together, they trained Cal AI using images from three different AI models. The app can now recognise both simple and complex foods, like sandwiches, mixed bowls, and packaged snacks. It has also learnt to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "estimate",
            "ref": "v-estimate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " how much food is on the plate by comparing photos to standard servings."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, Cal AI is 90% "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "accurate",
            "ref": "v-accurate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and it continues to improve thanks to user feedback. Since its "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "launch",
            "ref": "v-launch"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in May 2024, it has been downloaded over five million times. In February 2025 alone, the app earned over $2 million!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "One major factor for its success is social media. Zach reaches out to fitness influencers and asks them to talk about Cal AI. Their followers see the posts, try the app, and share it with others. As a result, it has gained particular popularity among users aged 15-25."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Zach graduated from high school this summer with top grades. Even though he has been accepted by several universities, he plans to take a gap year. He wants to make Cal AI even more accurate and help people of all ages eat more healthily. This young coder isn’t slowing down—he’s just getting started."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
